 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Perfect point complex",
 "statement": "In the Poincare duality conventions of this chapter (the fixed setting),\nobject $C$ of the\ncategory at the point is\n*perfect* if it is quasi-isomorphic to a bounded complex of finite\nprojective $A$-modules. The *derived dual* is\n$C^\\vee=R\\operatorname{Hom}_A(C,A)$, and the canonical evaluation and\ncoevaluation are the maps of the tensor–internal-Hom adjunction.",
